      "writtenOn": "2022-03-23T23:38:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The biggest concern I have with this code is that it seems to have implemented its own async runtime based around naive polling, and I don\u0027t see any justification for doing that.\n\nThe way I would recommend doing this would be to have a single-threaded tokio runtime manage your async pieces. This would simplify a lot of your code and avoid needing to validate subtle stuff with `Pin`/`Rc` - e.g. right now I think if you shut off the LinkManager while it still has a link active, you\u0027ll end up with it being alive forever.",
      "revId": "7823b3a924c0dcc29ca9d28e832fa1aa062d3f97",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5f364189_33fa6d3a",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-25T14:50:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "First, thank you for this very good review !\n\nThe implementation of the async runtime around naive polling is there mainly to have an interface compatible with the existing code of RootCanal where devices handle packet at the time they are polled in a `TimerTick` function.\n\nI don\u0027t think I would be able to fullfill this interface via a single-threaded tokio runtime as I would only be able to block and wait for a future to complete.\n\nFor the LinkManager you\u0027re right, thanks for catching that",
      "parentUuid": "a9669e8e_b00c59c0",
      "revId": "7823b3a924c0dcc29ca9d28e832fa1aa062d3f97",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
