      "lineNbr": 8,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-25T14:50:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I put this trait here to be able to give an alternative implementation of Context for testing. This is used on one of my commit of this chain `liblmp: Add tests from Bluetooth SIG LMP TestSuite`",
      "parentUuid": "d4e907ba_41df8ecf",
      "revId": "7823b3a924c0dcc29ca9d28e832fa1aa062d3f97",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cf414ec9_a5fe4e17",
        "filename": "tools/rootcanal/lmp/src/procedure/mod.rs",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1416371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-23T23:38:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If you\u0027re finding yourself manually implementing Future, and you\u0027re not writing a new async feature, that should be a red flag - in this case, specifically that you should probably just have each of your \"procedures\" have a message queue rather than all competing to yank packets out of a central cell.",
      "revId": "7823b3a924c0dcc29ca9d28e832fa1aa062d3f97",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "338d37d9_b11d1444",
        "filename": "tools/rootcanal/lmp/src/procedure/mod.rs",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-25T14:50:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In this case, I\u0027m manually implementing a Future mainly because I need a trait here and that we can\u0027t have async function in trait so I need a concrete future type.\nAs this was polling based I though it would be easier to create those smalls future types instead of using dynamic dispatch.",
      "parentUuid": "cf414ec9_a5fe4e17",
      "revId": "7823b3a924c0dcc29ca9d28e832fa1aa062d3f97",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c9cf4765_e00ec565",
        "filename": "tools/rootcanal/lmp/src/procedure/mod.rs",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 92,
      "author": {
        "id": 1416371
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-23T23:38:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, if I\u0027m reading this right you:\n1. Convert each expression into a repeated wait on that future, as a future.\n2. You create a future which will poll all of the sub-futures in a loop, assuming they can\u0027t terminate since they\u0027re in a loop.\n3. You wait on that future.\n\nIf that\u0027s correct, I think this obfuscates relative to just doing\n```\njoin! (\n  async { loop { authentication::initiate(\u0026ctx).await } },\n  async { loop { authentication::respond(\u0026ctx).await } },\n  ...\n);\n```",
      "revId": "7823b3a924c0dcc29ca9d28e832fa1aa062d3f97",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7cbac582_3edfb483",
        "filename": "tools/rootcanal/lmp/src/procedure/mod.rs",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 92,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881539
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-25T14:50:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are reading this right :)\n\nI would have used `join!` if I had access to the `futures_util` crate.\nBut RootCanal (that uses this library) is available as a test HAL, and so this lib needs to be `vendor_available`. Currently `futures_util` is not marked as `vendor_available`. The crate as multiple dependencies so I was not sure if making `vendor_available` was the right thing to do, could we make it available for `vendor` code ?",
      "parentUuid": "c9cf4765_e00ec565",
      "revId": "7823b3a924c0dcc29ca9d28e832fa1aa062d3f97",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
